{title: Is There Any Sorrow Like My Sorrow}
{subtitle: Lamentations 1:12}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Is it nothing to [Bb]you, [Ab]all you who pass [Eb]by
Look and [Bb]see
Is there [Cm]any sorrow like my [Gm]sorrow
That was [Ab]brought upon [Bb]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For these [Ab]things I [Eb]weep
My [Ab]eyes flow down with [Eb]tears
For the [Ab]comforter is [Cm]far from me
The [Ab]one who should restore my [Bb]soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Look and [Bb]see, [Cm]look and [Gm]see
[Ab]Is there any [Eb]sorrow like my [Bb]sorrow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My [Eb]children are [Bb]desolate
For the [Cm]enemy has pre[Gm]vailed
[Ab]Zion stretches out [Eb]her hands
And there [Ab]is none to comfort [Bb]her
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Eb] [Bb] | [Cm] [Gm] | [Ab] [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |
